All six features are implemented and verified. Here's what changed:

**`app/auth.py`** — `require_api_key` now reads the `X-API-Key` header, validates it against `VALID_API_KEYS`, and raises `HTTPException(401)` if missing or invalid. It returns the associated username on success.

**`app/main.py`** — Added the following endpoints and updated `GET /tasks`:
- `GET /tasks` — accepts optional query params `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` (combinable), plus `page` (default 1) and `page_size` (default 20). Returns the filtered, paginated slice.
- `POST /tasks` — requires auth via `Depends(require_api_key)`. Validates `project_id` against existing projects (404 if missing). Auto-generates the next unique integer ID and returns the created task with status 201.
- `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` — requires auth. Supports partial updates to `title`, `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` using `exclude_unset=True`. Returns 404 if the task doesn't exist.
- `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` — requires auth. Removes the task and returns 204; 404 if not found.

All endpoints follow the existing in-memory list + linear-scan pattern used in the codebase, and a run of the happy/unhappy paths passed.
